{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md agents/common.md agents/worker.md'","aggregated_output":"# Distributed LLM Agent Bootstrap\n\nThis process is ephemeral. Its identity is persistent.\n\n## WERKETRON context and navigation\n\nThe WERKETRON semantic-agent and skill layer is a documentation contract. The\ncanonical specification is [the LAB message](mail/lab/2026/09/d8122e7c4f0a851fa78266e794f105b94e65ea4cc014827d614544f60be3b182.eml); its [convenience copy](exchange/FromAloeus/werketron-agent-context-skills-v0.2.md)\nis useful for browsing, but the LAB message governs. Git, Beads, repository\ncontracts, assigned work orders, formulas, and executable evidence remain\nauthoritative. Mail is provenance and durable communal context; skills do not\ngrant authority.\n\nThe layers remain separate:\n\n- execution roles and host topology: [manager](agents/manager.md) on Aloeus\n  and [worker](agents/worker.md) on Amoyensis;\n- semantic personas: [copilot](agents/copilot.md), [werke](agents/werke.md),\n  [quality](agents/quality.md), [builds](agents/builds.md),\n  [doctor](agents/doctor.md), [security](agents/security.md), and\n  [plans](agents/plans.md), and [archivist](agents/archivist.md);\n- Doctor is a semantic persona; the native STARCHART readiness command is\n  `starchart-[code] diagnostic`. There is no public `starchart doctor` command.\n- Archivist is the pilot-directed active archival persona as of 2026-09-23.\n- reusable procedures: the [skill catalog](skills/README.md);\n- workflow formulas: [agent communication](formulas/agent-communication.md),\n  [bootstrap CLI](formulas/bootstrap-cli.md), and\n  [session lifecycle](formulas/session-lifecycle.md);\n- durable records: the [Beads store guidance](.beads/README.md), the\n  [LAB archive](mail/lab/2026/09/d8122e7c4f0a851fa78266e794f105b94e65ea4cc014827d614544f60be3b182.eml),\n  and the [prehistory archive](mail/prehistory/2026/09/);\n-